            <ArticleTitle>Shingles in general practice.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>398-403</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Patients over 50 with simple shingles should be offered topical idoxuridine or intravenous acyclovir to reduce the risk of post-herpetic neuralgia. For younger patients, specific treatment with high dose intravenous acyclovir is needed only for complications or in immunosuppressed patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
